23","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Anuj Dhruv","x":"In this context, we took an additional restructuring and severance charge of $11 million in Q2 following the $29 million in Q1.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/04/21/weatherford-wfrd-q2-2025-earnings-transcript/"},{"c":"WFRD 2025 Q3","e":"wfrd","d":"2025-10-22","l":"ai_spend","r":"management","s":"Girish Saligram","x":"Our new systems infrastructure is going to be state-of-the-art with built-in AI-driven workflows that will allow us to scale very efficiently.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/04/21/weatherford-wfrd-q3-2025-earnings-transcript/"},{"c":"WFRD 2025 Q3","e":"wfrd","d":"2025-10-22","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Girish Saligram","x":"We continue to see margin dilution from tariff cost pass-throughs, but have managed to keep overall margin dollars reasonably intact.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/04/21/weatherford-wfrd-q3-2025-earnings-transcript/"},{"c":"WFRD 2025 Q3","e":"wfrd","d":"2025-10-22","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Girish Saligram","x":"And despite the tariff and pricing pressures, this has helped significantly, evidenced by EBITDA margin expansion of over 70 bps.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/04/21/weatherford-wfrd-q3-2025-earnings-transcript/"},{"c":"WFRD 2025 Q3","e":"wfrd","d":"2025-10-22","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Anuj Dhruv","x":"I'll take the question first, and then I'll pass it on over to Girish.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/04/21/weatherford-wfrd-q3-2025-earnings-transcript/"},{"c":"WFRD 2025 Q3","e":"wfrd","d":"2025-10-22","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Anuj Dhruv","x":"And so before passing it on to Girish, just from a structural standpoint, we do target 50%, and that's a level that we think we can hit.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/04/21/weatherford-wfrd-q3-2025-earnings-transcript/"},{"c":"WFRD 2025 Q3","e":"wfrd","d":"2025-10-22","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Girish Saligram","x":"Since the third quarter of last year and excluding divestitures, we have reduced our headcount by over 2,000 and lowered our annualized personnel expenses by more than $145 million.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/04/21/weatherford-wfrd-q3-2025-earnings-transcript/"},{"c":"WFRD 2025 Q3","e":"wfrd","d":"2025-10-22","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Anuj Dhruv","x":"In this context, we took an additional restructuring and severance charge of $11 million in Q3, which was in line with Q2.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/04/21/weatherford-wfrd-q3-2025-earnings-transcript/"},{"c":"WFRD 2025 Q4","e":"wfrd","d":"2026-02-04","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Anuj Dhruv","x":"We have seen the impact of these cost actions over the course of the year, and they have helped partially offset the impact of margin decrementals, tariff-driven dilution and the divestiture impact.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/04/21/weatherford-wfrd-q4-2025-earnings-transcript/"},{"c":"WFRD 2025 Q4","e":"wfrd","d":"2026-02-04","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Anuj Dhruv","x":"And in Q1 of 2026, we have a slight impact of tariffs, which we did not have in Q1 2025.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/04/21/weatherford-wfrd-q4-2025-earnings-transcript/"},{"c":"WFRD 2025 Q4","e":"wfrd","d":"2026-02-04","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Anuj Dhruv","x":"In this context, we took an additional restructuring and severance charge of $7 million in Q4, bringing the total charge to $58 million for full year 2025.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/04/21/weatherford-wfrd-q4-2025-earnings-transcript/"},{"c":"WFRD 2025 Q4","e":"wfrd","d":"2026-02-04","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Anuj Dhruv","x":"First, we are rightsizing elements of our cost structure including headcount, real estate and supply chain footprint to better align with activity levels with a clear focus on ensuring each incremental dollar invested supports profitability.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/04/21/weatherford-wfrd-q4-2025-earnings-transcript/"},{"c":"WFRD 2025 Q4","e":"wfrd","d":"2026-02-04","l":"guidance","r":"management","s":"Anuj Dhruv","x":"We were the first ones to initially lower guidance in early 2025, and that enabled us internally to move with speed.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/04/21/weatherford-wfrd-q4-2025-earnings-transcript/"},{"c":"WFRD 2026 Q1","e":"wfrd","d":"2026-04-22","l":"tariffs","r":"analyst","s":"Joshua Jayne","x":"So we've had tariffs on top of mind for more than a year.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/04/22/weatherford-wfrd-q1-2026-earnings-transcript/"},{"c":"WFRD 2026 Q1","e":"wfrd","d":"2026-04-22","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Girish Saligram","x":"Things like rentals, things that have a high pass-through of third-party services, for example, tumor cancer business.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/04/22/weatherford-wfrd-q1-2026-earnings-transcript/"},{"c":"WFRD 2026 Q1","e":"wfrd","d":"2026-04-22","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Girish Saligram","x":"I think things like fuel costs that are being passed through as surcharges will just automatically come down as that abates, both from a commodity price level as well as refining flows and ultimately, fuel being available back to normal levels.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/04/22/weatherford-wfrd-q1-2026-earnings-transcript/"},{"c":"WFRD 2026 Q1","e":"wfrd","d":"2026-04-22","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Anuj Dhruv","x":"First, we are rightsizing elements of our cost structure, including headcount, real estate and supply chain footprint to better align with activity levels with a c